  correlation of SPAP between Doppler echocardiography and invasive RHC measurement. Pulmonary hypertension could be    
  diagnosed by echocardiography with high sensitivity and specificity."},                                               
          {"study_index": 44, "title": "Relevance of echocardiographic composite index to improve the detection of      
  pulmonary hypertension", "abstract": "Introduction and Objective :The transthoracic echocardiography (TTE) is         
  indicated for the detection of pulmonary hypertension (PH). The diagnosis is unlikely or probable according to a      
