  "Pulmonary artery systolic pressure (PASP) was assessed with simultaneous continuous wave Doppler echocardiography    
  (CW) and cardiac catheterization (CATH) in 33 cases. There was a close correlation between CW-estimated peak          
  pressure gradient of tricuspid regurgitation (TRPGp) and CATH-measured PASP (r= 0.96, P less than 0.0001). Excellent  
  correlation (r= 0.96, P less than 0.0001) between CW-estimated PASP and CATH-measured PASP was also obtained. The     
