│ PH.", "background": "Pulmonary hypertension (PH) is an important cause of morbidity and mortality, which leads to a  │
│ substantial loss of exercise capacity. PH ultimately leads to right ventricular overload and subsequent heart        │
│ failure and early death. Although early detection and treatment of PH are recommended, due to the limited            │
